    {
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Reflexive Verbs",
      "content_ref": null,
      "html": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #2E2A26;\">Many daily activities in Spanish use <strong>reflexive verbs</strong>. These describe things you do <em>to yourself</em>.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: #2E2A26;\">You add <strong>me</strong> before the verb:</p><div style=\"background: #DCE6E8; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 15px;\"><p style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #1B4B5A;\">levantarse → me levanto</p><p style=\"color: #2E2A26; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 14px;\">\"to get up\" → \"I get up\"</p></div><div style=\"background: #DCE6E8; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 15px;\"><p style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #1B4B5A;\">ducharse → me ducho</p><p style=\"color: #2E2A26; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 14px;\">\"to shower\" → \"I shower\"</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "A Morning Routine",
      "content_ref": null,
      "html": "<div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><p style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #1B4B5A;\">Me levanto a las siete.</p><p style=\"color: #2E2A26; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 14px;\">I get up at seven.</p></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><p style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #1B4B5A;\">Me ducho y me visto.</p><p style=\"color: #2E2A26; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 14px;\">I shower and get dressed.</p></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><p style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #1B4B5A;\">Desayuno café con tostadas.</p><p style=\"color: #2E2A26; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 14px;\">I have coffee and toast for breakfast.</p></div>"
    }
  ]
}